If you still have a Mac with an Intel chip inside, you're not going to want to pick up one of the new Studio Display or Studio Display XDR models.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/03/studio-display-and-xdr.jpg" alt="" width="1944" height="1094" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1038443" /><br/>
According to Apple's list of compatible Macs, neither model will work with an Intel-based Mac. Apple says that the Studio Display is compatible with a long list of Macs dating back to 2020, but they all have M-series chips inside.<br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li>16-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> (2021 and later)</li><br/>
 	<li>14-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; (2021 and later)</li><br/>
 	<li>13-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; (<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/m1/">M1</a>, 2020 and later)</li><br/>
 	<li>15-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-air/">MacBook Air</a> (2023 and later)</li><br/>
 	<li>13-inch &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; (&zwnj;M1&zwnj;, 2020 and later)</li><br/>
 	<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-studio/">Mac Studio</a> (2022 and later)</li><br/>
 	<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-mini/">Mac mini</a> (2020 and later)</li><br/>
 	<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-pro/">Mac Pro</a> (2023 and later)</li><br/>
 	<li>24-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/imac/">iMac</a> (2021 and later)</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
Apple started phasing out Intel Macs in 2020 when it released the first devices with Apple silicon. Intel chips were phased out in the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; in 2020 and &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; line in 2021, and other Macs followed. The last Intel Mac was the &zwnj;Mac Pro&zwnj;, and the Intel version was discontinued in 2023. Apple hasn't sold an Intel Mac for close to three years.<br/>
<br/>
With Intel Macs long discontinued, Apple is phasing out support as well. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-26/">macOS Tahoe</a> will be the final software update for Intel-based Macs, and Intel Macs will not get macOS 27. While Intel Macs will not be updated past &zwnj;macOS Tahoe&zwnj;, Apple plans to provide security updates for three additional years.<br/>
